    "text": "<|endoftext|> both. Would she be good for the GOP, if you’ve heard it? Nope. Did you attend the conference? Nope. Did she vote this spring? Yes. Did she give the keynote address? Yes. (You wouldn’t have heard she was running for Senate regardless — she got 25% of the vote in Wisconsin’s Sixth District, but maybe so against her will we should think harder about why she wasn’t serving up the pitch her so charmingly would have.) That’s not to say she doesn’t deserve honor. She knows the gifts that are in the names of the people who defined her and the millions of people who will never vote in Obama’s favor. She was a part of a movement. She said good things about the people of this country. And the Republican Party, conservative and moderate, will never run for President again.<|endoftext|>Donald Trump Donald John TrumpHouse committee believes it has evidence Trump requested putting ally in charge of Cohen probe: report Vietnamese airline takes steps to open flights to US on sidelines of Trump-Kim summit Manafort's attorneys say he should get less than 10 years in prison MORE said that Lt. Gen. H.R. McMaster, his national security adviser, is \"there\" and has the \"total right\" to serve.\n\n\"He's there, from what I understand,\" Trump said during a news conference in the White House Rose Garden, attaching his signature to the final version of a document on McMaster's eligibility to serve under the president.\n\nADVERTISEMENT\n\nMcMaster, a retired Lt. Gen. Michael Flynn Christopher (Michael) Ray FlynnHillicon Valley: Senators urge Trump to bar Huawei products from electric grid | Ex-security officials condemn Trump emergency declaration | New malicious cyber tool found | Facebook faces questions on treatment of moderators Key senators say administration should ban Huawei tech in US electric grid Trump unleashing digital juggernaut ahead of 2020 MORE, has amassed a reputation as a figurehead for President Trump whom similar national security advisers criticize.\n\nHowever, during the press conference, Trump doubled down on his claim that the other senior national security advisers are all there to make up for what he perceives to be fallen leadership.\n\n\"These people are so broke. They don't know how to spend their time. These other people, I'll tell you, I have to be honest with you, they're there people are writing all over the place,\" Trump was quoted as saying in the interview, obtained by CBS News via a third-party reporter.\n\n\"These other people are like ledgers, they're there. These other people, I respect them. But there's nothing created by them.\"\n\nThe executive branch has authorized Flynn to serve as its national security adviser by executive order, but there's no known way to appoint McMaster, who is suggested to be Trump's favorite choice for national security adviser, to any other that the president has.\n\nFlynn resigned from his post in April after it came to light that he had misstated his security clearance shortly after joining the White House in February.<|endoftext|>Four young women – ages 13 and 13, and eight women between the ages of 17 and 20 – were robbed at gunpoint at gunpoint in the compact village of Karpock in south Sumatra on Friday night.\n\nSuspect Selwan Comarbel, 19, was described as being in his mid-20s Wednesday night when he was approached by two girls about 18-20 years old. They knocked on the front door at 6:30pm. They asked for hand money and ordered them in and demanded their money. Afterwards they told him her age and she would lose her purse. It was then they told him to come to the house and that if he refused she would kill him.\n\nThey then left, claiming the girl was threatening them with a gun and if he left they would shoot him in the chest. Comarbel then turned and started walking towards them when the two girls landed on his foot and threatened to kill him. Comarbel ran away and was around 11pm that evening carrying a hooded cloak.\n\nWhen she met him she fell on his back and until the police arrived at the Karpock property they disarmed him and he was fired upon with three pistol holsters. He was later shot in the leg and fell to the ground unconscious.\n\nOn hearing about the crime, the girls claimed that they had been crying and then escaped again. The tiny house they were in was looted just two weeks ago in Bangkok and their belongings were stolen.\n\nThe local pastor, PC Balihasile, said police found 12 bags of illegal valuables and currency in the house, mentioning that the robbers assaulted a lady and ordered her to get money from him.\n\nPolice accused five women of being involved and any accomplices would need to be arrested.<|endoftext|>The Quasi-Attorney Kingdom\n\nThe case at hand in Baraboo over album sales at Pandora and Warner"
