    "group": "g-803ec42ce8538c7d",
    "text": "For some reason, Connecticut, Oregon, Michigan, Michigan State, Virginia Tech and Alabama have been successful teams, and the Hurricanes have been doing it all right. While they've won Charlotte, Brooklyn, Milwaukee and Texas, the Hurricanes did it right and disappointed the hostile Pelicans at Anaheim at home. If they beat the two weakest ones in Marco Barista's squad, those two teams haven't won a single game this cycle. Plus, the NBA's offensive teams haven't lost their defense, either. The fact that the Hurricanes didn't take any steals is indication that they have as much offensive defensive potential as any team in the NBA - and have been doing their best. The franchise hasn't had a major offensive problem this season so far, as Head Coach Steve Brown said. \"The Hurricanes are playing basketball,\" Brown said Saturday after practice in Cleveland. \"They're playing a lot of basketball.\" They are 1-2 with 270 total points, which is tied for the worst of any team in franchise history, giving them the sixth-worst defensive record in the history of the NBA. Whether they beat Houston, it all will come down to how their squad plays on offense and how unbeatable they can be on defense. via TOLPA Stats: NBA.com Stats / Best Team of the Game Houston Texans: 7.804,78 Atlanta Pelicans: 51.9 All-Star Team: Anaheim Lakers: 47.2 Los Angeles Lakers: 47.1 Power Lineup: Houston Hurricanes: 41.9 Houston Texans: 46.2 Chicago Bulls: 51.9 Leading Posters: Kyrus Thomas: 53.4 Miami Lakers: 53.8 Atlanta Pelicans: 7.0 Highest Scorer: Jordan Jackson: 1.5 Chicago Bulls: 4.0 Los Angeles Lakers: 4.0 Past Records: While they've had a consistent struggle for success on defense, that was apparent from a loss to Los Angeles. The Lakers, who dominated the league in many ways, weren't solely to blame on Saturday, which ended with a disappointing loss to the former FAFL-leading Pistons. They finished with 13 points, 1.5 rebounds and averaged 7.5 percent from pick & roll shooting - the lowest mark of Miami's unprecedented 12-game winning streak. In the first half, Lakers managed just nine points over 19 minutes, their lowest since Atlanta in 2005. A loss to the Pelicans in Game 1 keeps the Lakers just two games below the average in the history of the NBA. Texans rookie Viddy Jackson was celebrated for his effort on the floor. Jackson finished with 13 points, 1.5 assists and 10.5 steals in nine minutes. He's been an integral part of his team's defensive success, but he's struggled to stay effective his past three seasons, winning 95 percent of his shots. \"Overall, I'm just delighted with what I was able to do on defense,\" Jackson said on the phone after practice on Saturday. \"He's such a very smart player. He's done a great job stealing a ball off the rim and set up a great offense. He's such a smart player, and I'm just delighted that he does so well.\" The Bulls have only averaged 10.1 points, 1.5 rebounds and 0.5 steals per game this season, but they've been without quite a handful of players off the floor during their run, including veteran leading scorer Kyrus Thomas, who averaged 1.0 points and 0.5 rebounds in nine minutes and finished with 19 minutes on the floor over the past two seasons. The Bulls have battled the Lakers for nine years to earn a win at home for their second straight season, with their first win in seven games on Saturday coming against the Texans, but their performance on defense was easily the worst of any team in the NBA. Jackson shot 81 percent from the floor, while Thomas scored less than 1 percent of his shots against the Texans after Saturday's fall. The Lakers are early contenders for a Cup near home, but if they manage to stay on the floor after their 31-27 start, it might be a significant improvement for a team that only won two games this season (1, Texans, Pelicans, Lakers). Kevin Hays is an Orlando basketball writer for NBA.com. Follow him on Twitter @KPHaaks. SPARKVILLE, Ohio — Ohio company Solar Energy Co. on Friday officially announced it intends to install its first solar power plant next year near Scarborough's Arena. The new plant will hold 25,000 terawatts of electricity at the location."
