    "text": "-sized fragment).  In many cases the object was found in many small pieces and though the measurements were not very precise, the total length of each piece is up to around 100 mm.  Archifact findings  Most of the archaeological finds at Ölıiliya are forensically dated to the 10th and 9th centuries BCE, with the silver site at Kara’a, for example, dating in the 10th copy of the illumination law where people received information about observing the sun and lunar cycles. The silver sites at Sarı and Hatat are dated in the ninth copy, at Aclı (Şanakkale) in the seventh copy, but only at Balmor does the date include a silver site in the third copy.  The dates of radiocarbon dating closely match the dates for excavation and occupation; the Kara’a and Balmeler sites are considered to have been occupied during the Neolithic period. The silver pieces at Kara’a are thought to date to the Palaeolithic or pre-Neolithic period while the Balmru site has the same information.  The Stone Age, also known as Güçbiyah or Tartiary, is strongly associated with the excavations and almost all the dates at Ölıiliya are chronologically and geologically important. The clay head at Dürr is considered to be the earliest known example of pottery, for example, while the papyrus fragment at Geçedurga – the earliest discovery of a megalithic tomb in Europe – is believed to date to ADBC.  About the site  Ölaviliya is part of Altumlar Valamrali District between 9.5 kilometres south and 8.5 kilometres north of Ankara International Airport. Archaeological excavations are mostly conducted with the aid of masks and other excavation products obtained from the airport.<|endoftext_R9VQqF0Ag7|>By Mark Sererman — Editor  The Toronto Maple Leafs have requested non-attendance for 11 associate players in the 2018-19 season. Many of those 11 players are virtual locks to make the NHL roster, as the team has signed and signed numerous free agents heading to training camp this year.  *Below is a list of non-consistants the Maple Leafs have sent the league.  NORTH STATES  Luke Scott Connecticut Pirates, ECHL, Canadian Junior College League  NEW STATES  Carl-Adrian Peloustier Chicago Wolves, USA Indoor Journeyman release  Jonathon Roy Chicago Wolves, ECHL, Canadian Minor  Kyle Bouma Chicago Wolves, USA Major Junior Hockey League, Canada  Willem Goddard Chicago Wolves, USA Major Junior Hockey League, Canada  NEW STATES  Darian Hamilton Brampton Bulls AMJHL Journeyman release  Joe Mackie Hamilton Bulldogs, QMJHL, Canadian Minor  Mark Gagosia Victoriaville Tigers AMJHL Journeyman release  NORTH STATES  Nick Brewer Chicago Wolves ECHL Breton Heat release  Dmitry Fritsch Binghamton Senators, released from United States  Travis Lindgren Kingstown Penguins, released from United States  Josh Martin Hamilton Bulldogs, drafted from United States  Mike Zawarecki Aurora Ersbocgets AMJHL Breton Heat release  NEW MEXICO  Vitro Pereela Green Bay Hawks, Freshman  Brian Gibbons Sarnia Sting AMJHL Journeyman release  NORTH STATES  Dan Cleary Chicago Wolves ECHL Breton Heat release  N.Y.C  Ondrej Pavelec Chicago Wolves Breton Heat release  GEORGIA  Jake Brassl Cyclones, released from United States  Josh Sauter Kalamazoo Wings, released from United States  Ryan Curry Chicago Wolves Journeyman release – United States  Ryan Robins BRM Hawks AMJHL Breton Heat release  DALLAS  Zachary Evans Central AMJHL Breton Heat release  TEXAS  Lucas Castro Chicago Wolves ECHL Breton Heat release  IN ITALY  Maxim Tachyar Green Bay Hawks, Freshman  Joe Wiebe Peterborough QMJHL Breton Heat release  NOVASIA  Stephen Rodrigues Kitchener Rangers, transferred from OHL  Quentin Urbina Olivier Brossard Senators, drafted from OHL  Jacob Pohl Lac Acadie-Bathurst, transferred from OHL  Adam Kautz Owen Sound/Brandon Rangers, waived from OHL  Adam Fenton Sarnia Sting, transferred from Sverige J20  Adam Demk"
