    "text": "PC) said donations were allowed for businesses earning SGD 100,000, SGD 200,000, SGD 200,000, SGD 300,000, and SGD 500,000 annually per business category. Any business with an annual income of less than 10 million SGD had to apply for subsidies, according to ABS-CBN.  Gayo-Star and most broadcast stations in Metro Manila have been sponsoring some of their channels free of charge due to the lack of funding in recent months.  \"We have consistently faced difficulties in our industry given the spread of the coronavirus pandemic. While we have had to already secure some financial incentives provided to filmmakers and producers, this resolution allows us to provide further assistance free of service fee to program makers in exchange for respecting restrictions at filming locations, monitoring the activities of artists, and monitoring public sources,\" said Mr. Oscar de Castro C. Aquino from the film and television RCDA.  The Commission also announced that changes will be made to everyone's account information, such as company address, telephone number, ID card, etc., until further notice related to qualifying residents and interested travelers to self-isolate from effective March 1, 2020 until May 31. The Secretary said such measures are intended to encourage people to observe six-feet distancing and other public health guidelines.  Under the measures, all inmates starting May 31 are not eligible to apply for an extension for any condition on bail, for which they must apply for a waiver in advance and exercise their right to appeal. They may still apply forfeiting bail, but only in certain cases.<|endoftext_R9VQqF0Ag7|>“Altcoins continue to maintain active markets that attract traders willing to take risk by investing in the highest value assets.”  The altcoin markets have demonstrated remarkable resilience despite failing to closely follow the stock market index in 2017. As has been an ongoing trend, price-valuation indicators on most benchmarks have remained relatively stable. While overall volume has decreased, altcoins continue to maintain active markets that attract traders willing to take risk by investing in the highest value assets. The mature industry has made significant strides in the fields of technology and regulation, and in this way remains uniquely positioned to survive the periodic market cycles present in the stock markets.  The different altcoin exchange mechanisms provide an alternative framework to the conventional markets that allows specific speculative mechanisms to emerge and thrive, and simultaneously features enough liquidity to withstand extreme price movements. These structures also provide a unique opportunity to develop and implement smart contracts for smart collateral to allow for the emergence of decentralized finance.  General Sale for Bid  General sales for bid are specialized exchanges that cater exclusively to altcoin speculators. These exchanges are bid on to acquire altcoin tokens for future delivery at the prevailing rate on the bitcoin market that altcoin tokens have established. Unlike exchanges that transact regular shares immediately, these sales typically use spot order designs that have already been used by past spot-order sales. Auction sales for bid also typically incorporate escrow or price guarantee contracts for very low trading volumes; this is because extremely high volumes would result in significant transaction costs and render the auction volumes unbalanced.  Spread Sale-Ask Auctions  Unlike sales for bid, split bid-order exchanges are designed to sell specific values, typically valued at a 5% premium over spot value. Lit bid-order exchanges generally use similar or identical rules and procedures to scalping exchanges, but in addition provide a purchase price below the current value of bitcoin to prevent speculative trading. By avoiding the price of the spot market, split bid-order exchanges are cheaper than sales that use purchase order designs. Flat bid order exchange designs are used in many currently operating smart bid exchanges, supporting the popularity of this still obscure market structure.  Auctions for Smart Bid  Smart bid exchanges are based on a smart contract to unlock the ability to purchase tokens at a specified future price. Unlike scalping exchanges where you have to provide and maintain fiat capital, these smart bid exchanges offer bids on the future price of an altcoin as well as on the value of the token itself. Instead of creating value out of thin air or using an arbitrary pricing mechanism, you are using a smart contract to base your position on actual future prices of bitcoin. Though usually designed by and for altcoin traders exclusively, smart bid exchanges are the precursors of bid order exchanges, and are also designed to accommodate flexible and relatively low barriers to entry, including escrow contracts if desired.  Though these smart bid exchanges are typically small-scale and niche, they increase market liquidity by providing institutional traders with the ability to purchase altcoin tokens at prices above the current value.  General Bond Actions  Bond bond contracts protect altcoin exchanges against bankruptcy should the collateral value fall below a specified level. General bond contracts are often used on scalping exchanges to keep the trend alive. As systems security protocols become more sophisticated, general bond contracts are rapidly growing in use on altcoin exchanges.  Oracle Contract Auctions"
