    "group": "g-15849cd60e30402b",
    "text": "top banks to do everything they can to rig the system in their favor.  The purposeful demolulation of economic activity could not have been more blatant—and the system no more corrupt. It is the same strategy the Obama administration used when seizing subprime mortgages in 2010. Seizing them was swift and required guarantees of heavy losses by financial firms, as well as a threat to cut the dividends paid to the investors if the firms went bankrupt. Such an alternative would be the disincentive to keep lending to the subprime mortgages that now drive the nation’s burgeoning mortgage crisis.  For any economic proposal to win support across the board, and across the political spectrum, it requires dramatic improvements in the lives of millions of working people and the young people who would otherwise inherit the credit. The Democratic Party must abandon its commitment to defending the interests of financial elites and lead the effort to mobilize wealth to provide significant public investment and equal opportunity. A struggle for basic human dignity does not accept cues from big business or the stock markets. The independent resistance of the working class and young people must lead it.<|endoftext_R9VQqF0Ag7|>Korda's comments come following statements by US Congress that state-sponsored hackers had managed to hack into the emails of the oil giant. Chief Executive Joe Laidlaw. Credit:LIKEUP \"We continue to be confident in the strength of our security, particularly as a result of the fact that we have implemented industry leading security processes in our latest 15-month-long internal review, which was completed in June 2016,\" she said.  A BP employee walks through metal detectors at the main security entrance at BP Shell Humphreys-Hilkesdale. Credit:Getty Images Deloitte, which was re-established in 2006, has focused much of its services on financial information. In 2014 the company had its best year ever, taking home a record $1.1 billion in revenues and profits. It expects the company will generate $1.2 billion in revenue this year. Since its re-establishment a decade ago, Deloitte has expanded its operations globally and employs more than 10,000 people in the US, Europe and Asia. The company also has $5 trillion in assets under management. Typhoon hackers first gained unauthorized access to BP Chief Financial Officer Richard Kronig on November 9, 2015, and sent a copy of his login password from a client file to a phishing site.    Armed with the password and the login details, the hackers managed to find out information about the entire staff at the complex, exposing the names and emails, and passwords of senior members of staff, board members and technical advisors. Last year, the accounts of congressmen and military officials were also breached, including the Washington Governor Jay Inslee and more than 20 other politicians from both sides of the aisle. \"Deloitte has systems in place to strengthen the security of information in emails. Additional security systems are also implemented in order to protect the integrity of information and the integrity and integrity of computer systems,\" Korda said. US Senator Jeff Merkley told Reuters that America should be concerned that the attackers are no longer working in simulations and are now dealing with the way the real world operates. \"The threat is real for now,\" he said earlier at a hearing on hacking in the U.S. Congress. \"Through illegal hacking through the National Security Agency and through espionage, the Russians were able to take control of our reliance on critical infrastructure, our water and electric grid.\" Russia's government also took down grid.  BP internal review ordered  BP said that the breach of information was still under investigation and that the company was working closely with the FBI to determine how it had been breached and what did it mean. Hackers breached the accounts of American politicians and Washington's governor Jay Inslee. Credit:Hannah Caldwell/Getty Images \"BP cannot confirm or deny a criminal breach because the matter is currently under investigation. This matter is the subject of a continuing investigation by the FBI, which is being fully cooperated by its economic crime division,\" the company said. Laidlaw was the first and final person to comment on the matter.<|endoftext_R9VQqF0Ag7|>As more than 100 wildfires continue to burn in wilderness across Northern California following low temperatures, shifts in weather patterns could make future blazes even more dangerous a threat, authorities say.  Winter variation complicates California’s ability to manage local fire weather to fulfill its desired mission to prevent or contain wildfires, a factor noted by forecasters forecasting summer weather even more intense than the conditions that prevailed this winter.  The fires came six quarters into a fire season that ended in early 2017 and went dormant until early this year as many areas experienced drought followed by fire. It was the hottest period that year since 2000, according to the U.S. Geological Survey.  Officials reported 471 wildfires across the Northern California from November to April, more than double the same period a year ago.  Advertisement  The fires were fueled by winds blowing in the"
