    "text": "of travels in different places around Mumbai city and looking for an efficient, professional yet economical solution? Our services at each unit provide great creativity and care so that your specific needs are understood well and met with tranquillity. Apart from the beautifully curated accommodation experience at Ravi-Kurri, we also offer an extensive range of services for our dedicated concierge.  Our rooms are made from the highest quality materials and take pride to provide exceptional services that ignite the spirits of our guests. Our ergonomic shape and height, customized furniture and decor, attractive designs and choice of international materials throw off the natural vibe and give our concierge a mind-blowing ambiance that makes our guests fall in love with us.  We would like to give due credit to our professional staff who provide us with information on how to carry out all legal procedures on all services and are always ready to respond for our guest. Also, our mobile connectivity is compatible with all modern cell phones.<|endoftext_R9VQqF0Ag7|>LOS ANGELES — Foreign governments, businesses and individuals have built a new line of defense to protect their communications from potential spies, examining every email, chat session and electronic message that might be left under their coverage.  A New York law school hosted a debate on Wednesday about whether we should expect lawyers to do the same.  “Is it appropriate to expect a law firm to engage in an eavesdrop on a client’s private communication?” asked Melissa A. Goldberg, a dean and associate professor at the Bancroft School of Law at the City University of N.Y.-N.Y., during a talk about software that Accenture makes.  Among other things, Accenture’s SecureMark software decrypts multiple data sent through a tool called ContactKey by noting that a name was typed on a computer’s keyboard or associated with the names of friends using e-mail — a trick made possible by the National Security Agency’s surveillance program and approved by Congress, under a law called the Electronic Communications Privacy Act.<|endoftext_R9VQqF0Ag7|>Get breaking news alerts and special reports. The news and stories that matter, delivered weekday mornings.  An Israeli soldier suffered severe bruising and swelling to one of the fingers on his right hand during \"March of Return\" protests near the Gaza border when a human shield was formed to disperse them with tear gas, the military said Tuesday.  Mor Gilad Levi was hurt during the clashes at Mount Zion, a demonstration that the military said was aimed at stopping rockets in Gaza in which scores of protesters threw rocks and stones at Israeli security forces while burning tires.  The 28-year-old soldier was receiving medical care from breathing problems and fractured ribs, according to media reports.  Gaza demonstrators throw stones at Israeli troops during clashes on 2nd day of closure of fence at the Gaza border, east of Rafah, May 24, 2018. Maan News Agency  Video footage released by the military shows clashes at the moment the soldiers defied protesters' call to disperse the crowds by blasting them with tear gas.  ולבשנביה תרתות מלות הים החרלמות שבות הניההלות ברה עלחחורת בלה ישיל שנות מנוחהרבית ה להלים pic.twitter.com/cRyKdZ1Oxn — ‏ IDF (@IDFupdated) May 24, 2018  Israel opened fire just before and during the \"March of Return\" protests near Gaza's besieged coastal enclave on Monday. At the time, it said this prevented an incursion on the border fence. But Palestinians claim an Israeli armored vehicle was struck with a stone.  Resistance Front men set fire as Palestinians demonstrate in Beit Hanoun after the military opened fire in the enclave. AP Photo/Peter Galagros  King was also injured in the clashes when his niece nearby hurled a stone. The Israeli military later determined the soldiers were hit by a rock.  Hamas spokesman Fawzi Barhoum praised the wounded soldier, saying he was attempting to form a human shield against the Palestinian protesters when he lost his hand.  \"Everyone’s dignity and everyone’s life will be lost if they attempt to crush and prevent the legitimate goals and legitimate aspirations of the people,\" Barhoum said.  Military paramedics said Levi was evacuated to nearby Beit Hanoun after suffering severe wounds, but he was declared still alive at another hospital."
