    "text": "a tough appearance and when we see his bust in museum he’s turned out in something much more modern and pretty cool. The figure certainly doesn’t look as good as previous series’ in its more tattered armor but at this price point the look is pretty acceptable and I can see it appealing to some younger fans too.  LIMITED WEAPONS  Alongside the figure we get two other neat upgrades for Iron Man. The MSA series got another starter kit that came in the form of a tote. This gave you not just his sword and armor but also his visor to use that gear in combat and a hazmat helmet.  This set gives him a shield and a stylish suit that fits you his body. It honestly doesn’t seem like it’s related in any way to his actual suit since this figure has it more focused on the strength of the figure, but the accessory component of the suit is quite nice. Plus it helps that it fits securely and goes on the figure with enhanced ease which fits his body well.  His last big upgrade is invulnerability. Iron Man has a small energy belt on his chest area that he draws energy from to help extend his abilities as a superhero. The suit is only 11cm in length.  NEED TO GROW  This figure has a lot going going for him. The posing is pretty good too, but as previously mentioned I really want some more accessories on this figure so that he can lug his stuff around for longer. Its not unreasonable to want them to add a few more items like outright a hammer and even some wire to keep him safe. It’s also nice to see him with weapons in both hands and a secondary weapon too.  FEATURES  As you probably know the main method of healing Iron Man in the comic is his conveyor bolts. The original protector bolts were kind of awkward for the original series, and while the heat effect was good the way they extended out the joint wasn’t quite as effective.  To remedy this we now have him with some support legs hidden inside his suit. These are both perfectly fine and could easily be used with other figures as well. He also gets some form of arm grabber ability, where rather than extending his full to the ground he can throw his lower arm upwards. Unfortunately it honestly isn’t too impressive and not really part of the collection.  CONCLUSION  This figure has so much promise as Iron Man and I really want to build him up with some better accessories but with Hasbro Classics being able to sell this well built figure at a very affordable price it’s hard to see this figure standing out. At minimum he should be given a few extra bolts or energy cones so he can lug stuff around for longer or maybe help make other figures easier to use. While overall the line is a pretty good one it’s just not good enough to be worth being part of a larger lineup of figures. We have action figures of some great core characters and this one is worth looking at for those who just want a decent amount of accessories.  Leave your questions, comments and recommendations with me here on Facebook Comment and Tweet me @sonicde or @mysticionymaofthego  -  Iron Man: Hasbro Classics | Marvel    SPONSOR SPOT ABOUT THE NUTSHIP:  LEGO has up their game with these new items  105 Scale Iron Man Collection → $20 Buy Now at Amazon  1235 Captain America → $8 at Amazon  760 TRON Legacy → $24 Buy Now at Amazon<|endoftext_R9VQqF0Ag7|>Ned Stark, the Lannister heir apparent in George R.R. Martin’s beloved epic Game of Thrones, is the subject of a new graphic novel from IDW. This prequel book will be written by writer F. Ramón González with art and story Luciano Rivera and is called Hanlan’s Trap, book 2 of the Blood and Chrome trilogy. We’ve spoken with Chip Zdarsky to create our exclusive preview for the new novel. It includes information on the story, the design behind the characters, and so much more. Let’s begin!  Sir Ned Stark is one of the best characters we have ever had in Westeros. He went through endless trials and almost death and managed to emerge mostly intact. What can you tell us about this warrior in the Blood and Chrome graphic novel?  Cook Zdarsky: Having the series take place in the Star Wars mythos is a blessing in disguise. I researched and wrote a treatment that makes it clear that this is a Star Wars graphic novel. The basic concept is simple. An unknown Cardassian smuggler slips landing on his home planet. A new Cardassian detective attempts to figure out the conflict that may be driving his actions, and"
